From 7bd750d0c3dbdb1b77f3cc3e0c9a7bc010bb8aa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 03:48:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 193/217] perf(cuda-w8a8): rewrite quantize_per_token_s8 as
 block-per-row (R6)

The C6 timing evidence (9ad9d4801) measured quantize_per_token_s8 at
0.29-1.03 ms per call on the RTX 5080, 84.7-92.2% of the full W8A8 op,
because kernel version 1 ran one serial thread per row (m=1/5 -> 1/5
active threads) with a per-element div.rn.f64 + cvt.rni.s32.f64.

Rewrite (numeric semantics unchanged):

- one 128-thread block per row (grid.x == rows);
- absmax via local max.f32 + warp shfl.sync.down + 64 B shared/bar.sync
  tree; max.f32 is exact and order independent, so the absmax and the
  div.rn.f32(absmax, 127.0f) scale are bit-identical to kernel v1;
- per-element rounding keeps the RNE decision of cvt.rni.s32.f64 without
  an f64 division: div.rn.f32 -> cvt.rni.s32.f32 candidate + an exact
  fma.rn.f64 residual (d = x - n*scale), then 2|d| vs scale decides the
  half-way case.  The old f64 quotient is within 2**-45 of the exact ratio
  while a nonzero distance to a half boundary is >= 2**-25, so both agree
  bit-for-bit on finite inputs;
- zero-row (scale 1.0, codes 0), NaN/Inf (status 1), scale underflow
  (status 2) and the saturation counter keep their exact write-back
  conventions.

Runtime/harness: the quantize launch domain becomes rows*CUDA_W8A8_BLOCK
(grid.x == rows); the other three opcodes are untouched.  The c6 timing
harness and its selftest mirror the geometry (the only measurement-
instrument change).  New scripts/perf/c6_quantize_bitdiff.py renders the
base-tree PTX and the rewritten PTX and diffs codes/scales/saturation/
status byte-for-byte on the device (58 cases / 73,256 elements / 45
shapes, full-buffer SHA256).

Evidence (see the task evidence dir for raw files):

- old-vs-new differential: 58/58 PASS on sm_120; 206 corpus elements
  would change code under a plain f32 quotient, and the residual path
  keeps them identical;
- independent verify-qwen35-w8a8-gpu-kernels harness: 121/121 PASS;
- 12-shape cuEvent medians (R=51, warmup=5): 289-1034 us -> 11.2-22.2 us,
  19-50x (median 24x).  All numbers UNGATED: the GamePC window was shared
  (GPU util median 71.5-73.5%) and the rate gate failed, so the speedup
  is a magnitude-level, conservative lower bound.
- local full pytest python/tests/ut/pypto_x: 1268 passed / 7 skipped /
  0 failed (base collects 1269, this tree 1275 = base + 6 new tests).
