+      (``status = 2``) conventions are unchanged;
+    * **per-element rounding** still reproduces ``cvt.rni.s32.f64(x /
+      scale)`` bit-for-bit without an f64 division.  ``div.rn.f32`` gives the
+      correctly rounded f32 quotient ``q32`` (within ``2**-24`` relative of
+      the exact ratio), ``cvt.rni.s32.f32`` gives a candidate integer, and the
+      exact residual ``d = x - n*scale`` is formed with a single exact
+      ``fma.rn.f64``; comparing ``2|d|`` against ``scale`` decides the RNE
+      tie/near-tie case.  A nonzero ``|q - (k+0.5)|`` is bounded below by
+      ``2**-25`` while the f64 quotient error is below ``2**-45``, so this
+      reproduces the old f64 decision exactly;
+    * NaN/Inf still fail closed with ``status = 1`` and write nothing else.
